<title> Lesson Activities</title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list>
  <item>4.17.1: Define a Sequence</item>
  <item>4.17.2: What Is a Recursive Definition?
    <list>
      <item>4.17.2: Self Check</item>
      <item>
        4.17.2: Additional Resources
      </item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>4.17.3: Ways to Represent a Sequence
    <list>
      <item>4.17.3 Self Check</item>
      <item>
        4.17.3: Additional Resources
      </item>
    </list>
  </item>
  <item>4.17.4: Geometric Recursive Definitions</item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 4.17.5: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<list>
  <item>
    Graph paper
  </item>
  <item>
    Pre-printed slips, cut from copies of the blackline master, card sort
  </item>
</list>
<title>Required Preparation</title>
<list>
  <item><link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b1c7f45ea61e04576f803579e40435991820b355">Cut card sort for activity</link> (enough for each pair).
  </item>
</list>
<title> Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para>During this lesson, it is important to:</para>
<list>
  <item>
    Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. Encourage students to look for these words and notice their use and meanings.
  </item>
  <item>
    Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and their written and oral explanations.
  </item>
  <item>
    Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link>
  </item>
</list>
<para>Vocabulary words that are emphasized in this lesson include:</para>
